cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pilitrack: reproducible quantification of type-IV pili dynamics"
message: "If you use pilitrack in your research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Baffour Awuah"
    given-names: "Michael"
keywords:
  - "type-IV pili"
  - "T4P"
  - "TIRF microscopy"
  - "filament tracking"
  - "microbiology"
  - "bioimage analysis"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/"
abstract: >-
  pilitrack quantifies type-IV pili (T4P) dynamics from fluorescence
  microscopy time-lapses: per-pilus length, extension and retraction
  velocity, number of piliated cells, and pili per cell. It provides
  reproducible, provenance-tracked analysis (input and output checksums,
  recorded software versions and numerical environment), a browser and a
  desktop app, and a detect->correct->retrain labeling workflow.
